course: dictionary
lesson: 8423
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Rusty is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «Things left out in the rain go rusty and wear out sooner» is about metal, because rain and wear are things that happen to iron and steel.
explain: «My French is rusty» has nothing to do with metal. Rusty here means you are not as good at something as you used to be, because you have not practised it for a long time. The clue is French: you can't rust a language, but you can get out of practice.
explain: Some clues are about colour. «The rusty black bonnet» uses rusty to mean reddish-brown, like rust. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Rusty has three meanings: covered in rust, out of practice, and reddish-brown in colour.
fact: Rust is a reddish-brown, flaky coating that forms on iron and steel when they get wet and meet the air.
fact: Rusting is a chemical reaction: iron, water and oxygen make rust.
fact: Paint, oil, plastic coatings and galvanising stop metal from rusting.
fact: After a cut from a rusty nail, tell an adult, because you may need a tetanus injection, a jab against a dangerous germ.
exercise: «A rusty nail actually weighs more than a clean one.» Why does it weigh more? | Lost iron to the water | *It has gained oxygen from the air | It has shrunk in the heat | It has been dipped in paint
exercise: Jayden says, «My French is rusty.» What does rusty mean here? | Covered in flaky reddish coating | Very fast and sharp | *Not as good as before, because he has not practised | Reddish-brown in colour
exercise: Which stops metal from rusting? | Scratching it with a stone | *Galvanising | Keeping it wet every day | Leaving it out in the rain
test: In «Things left out in the rain go rusty and wear out sooner», what does rusty mean? | *Covered in rust | Very shiny | Reddish-brown in colour | Out of practice
test: What should you do after a cut from a rusty nail? | Put a plaster on and say nothing | Lick it clean | Wash it and forget it | *Tell an adult, because you may need a tetanus injection
exam: Ella says, «My maths is a bit rusty since the summer.» What does she mean? | Her maths is covered in rust | *She needs practice, because she is not as good as before | She has done too much maths | Her maths book is reddish-brown
